owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-29T19:18:59Z","updated_at":"2016-05-29T19:18:59Z","body":"Sure, I can take a look at this. I did come across similar problems while trying to get it to work with process isolation. I'd very much appreciate some feedback on some various workarounds that I had come up with and their various shortcomings:\n1. Create a temporary file with the job code and require it in the coverage template. Problem: This will cause an include loop with PHPTs that test process isolation as `PHPUnit_Util_GlobalState::getIncludedFilesAsString()` will include this temporary file and there doesn't appear to be an easy way to blacklist this temp file.\n2. Adjust the coverage template and use the `auto_prepend_file` ini directive to handle the coverage generation and saving.\n   Problem: This will prevent PHPT tests from utilizing this directive in their INI sections\n\nI had the ground work laid for 1, but didn't couldn't get around the process isolation issue.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sebastianbergmann/phpunit/issues/comments/222377666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kabel","id":675956,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NTk1Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/675956?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel","html_url":"https://github.com/kabel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kabel/followers","following_url":"https://api.